{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 469 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "6d5f0d81d7ef64051628053ff4dd8396e5808a20c68ea3673c267855c882f8eb" :edb/db-before-t 468 :edb/db-after-t 469 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533781 50 #inst "2026-10-04T22:55:29.210Z" 13194139533781 true] [17592186184092 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250655 13194139533781 true] [17592186184092 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250676 13194139533781 true] [17592186184092 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250704 13194139533781 true] [17592186184093 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250683 13194139533781 true] [17592186184093 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250690 13194139533781 true] [17592186184093 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250697 13194139533781 true] [17592186184093 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250711 13194139533781 true] [17592186184177 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250641 13194139533781 true] [17592186184177 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250648 13194139533781 true] [17592186184177 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250662 13194139533781 true] [17592186184177 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250669 13194139533781 true] [17592186184769 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533781 true] [17592186184769 1145 "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\pi -(-\\pi )=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n2\\pi =\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{2\\pi }=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ unit up. Hence, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+1.\n$$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186184772 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533781 true] [17592186184772 1145 "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}=5.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{3}{2}$ units up. Hence, $D=\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, $B-2D=5-2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2})=5-3=2.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5x)+\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186184773 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533781 true] [17592186184773 1145 "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}(x+2C))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+2C$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}(x+2C))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=tan\\,(\\frac{x}{2}).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/8a19beac86998c845d7ffa225a52d425ab48b9ec350f6c8fe42f7c6dbce027ce.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})$ by $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ units to the left. Therefore:\n\n$$\n2C=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{\\pi }{8}\n$$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186184787 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533781 true] [17592186184787 1145 "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}=3.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $3$ units up. Hence, $D=3.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=3+3=6.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)+3.\n$$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250641 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250642 13194139533781 true] [17592186250641 1089 "q-117795" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250641 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533781 true] [17592186250641 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/0f920d90aa215300e720ace10bfec9292440d20f32c9b907854b984014f77427.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250641 1113 #uuid "e52e5ebc-a1b0-593c-b883-50f2676ea209" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250641 1145 "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}=3.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $3$ units down. Hence, $D=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=3+(-3)=0.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)-3.\n$$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250643 13194139533781 true] [17592186250642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250644 13194139533781 true] [17592186250642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250645 13194139533781 true] [17592186250642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250646 13194139533781 true] [17592186250642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250647 13194139533781 true] [17592186250642 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533781 true] [17592186250642 1041 "selection" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250642 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250645 13194139533781 true] [17592186250642 1110 #uuid "f8782fa4-99e0-56ca-9e87-9316a4149688" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250643 1034 "3" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250643 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250643 1111 #uuid "e9802eb8-3fbe-5dec-a5a2-e38dcba2d37c" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250644 1034 "2" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250644 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250644 1111 #uuid "43c95071-cc23-5c59-85e9-6847e9350c15" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250645 1034 "0" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250645 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250645 1111 #uuid "04bcb005-98cd-5cad-b7d8-009b96a173e9" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250646 1034 "-1" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250646 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250646 1111 #uuid "56204d13-e746-5592-8848-2dc92e919d8e" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250647 1034 "-2" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250647 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250647 1111 #uuid "5d9f969d-cf1d-51f1-ab5a-72431daf59ad" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250648 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250649 13194139533781 true] [17592186250648 1089 "q-117796" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250648 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533781 true] [17592186250648 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/9278723975d70fec73e313d0e164908ddd339231cb74f75b07c2edce14680111.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250648 1113 #uuid "5ecbe368-922d-5a9f-956d-5a27886e10df" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250648 1145 "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}-(-\\frac{2\\pi }{5})=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{4\\pi }{5})}=\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{1}{2}$ unit up. Hence, $D=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5x}{4})+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250650 13194139533781 true] [17592186250649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250651 13194139533781 true] [17592186250649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250652 13194139533781 true] [17592186250649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250653 13194139533781 true] [17592186250649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250654 13194139533781 true] [17592186250649 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533781 true] [17592186250649 1041 "selection" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250649 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250651 13194139533781 true] [17592186250649 1110 #uuid "6606a1ed-6024-5de9-8007-316331c1b133" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250650 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250650 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250650 1111 #uuid "2d6103da-a933-5f3c-8237-e5d132840235" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250651 1034 "\\frac{7}{4}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250651 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250651 1111 #uuid "92860296-dfb3-5191-91ee-b4a0c5141c29" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250652 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250652 1111 #uuid "337dced6-8a5a-546e-b2e9-0a32904fde55" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250653 1034 "3" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250653 1111 #uuid "8b11421c-f405-508e-a3c5-f0e8804caa0a" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250654 1034 "4" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250654 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250654 1111 #uuid "119f49a0-bc34-50b8-b276-600854b8e6b5" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250655 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250656 13194139533781 true] [17592186250655 1089 "q-117800" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250655 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533781 true] [17592186250655 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/6003a85e0038b7e6562381cd338a7597877d1152adbeb476b7141eee74ba06ee.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250655 1113 #uuid "c44f6521-15eb-5c8e-93a8-cab320c1122a" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250655 1145 "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}-0=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{2\\pi }{5})}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{5}{4}$ units up. Hence, $D=\\frac{5}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{5}{4}=\\frac{15}{4}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})+\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250657 13194139533781 true] [17592186250656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250658 13194139533781 true] [17592186250656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250659 13194139533781 true] [17592186250656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250660 13194139533781 true] [17592186250656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250661 13194139533781 true] [17592186250656 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533781 true] [17592186250656 1041 "selection" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250656 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250661 13194139533781 true] [17592186250656 1110 #uuid "091351e4-7a45-5333-a5a0-b28f52c127a3" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250657 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250657 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250657 1111 #uuid "3f8ae70b-92d9-5cc9-a5be-dd6531ddc6dc" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250658 1034 "\\frac{11}{4}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250658 1111 #uuid "168b009b-eb74-530b-9138-85aec12ac989" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250659 1034 "\\frac{13}{2}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250659 1111 #uuid "6a2b64b3-85a3-5025-be6e-aafff2391545" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250660 1034 "\\frac{13}{4}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250660 1111 #uuid "96fa204e-098d-5cda-9798-e6c188251b83" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250661 1034 "\\frac{15}{4}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250661 1111 #uuid "07bc4b07-a41a-563e-9c73-730b3c518709" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250662 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250663 13194139533781 true] [17592186250662 1089 "q-141974" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250662 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533781 true] [17592186250662 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/2b8bbc9ae6b8bf8c441c8e2b534fb159f8180833e1891baa094f988d6a362117.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $D-B?$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250662 1113 #uuid "fc965e10-4874-590e-8c18-9692661389da" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250662 1145 "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=\\frac{6\\pi }{4}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ units up. Hence, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $D-B=1-(\\frac{2}{3})=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})+1.\n$$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250664 13194139533781 true] [17592186250663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250665 13194139533781 true] [17592186250663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250666 13194139533781 true] [17592186250663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250667 13194139533781 true] [17592186250663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250668 13194139533781 true] [17592186250663 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533781 true] [17592186250663 1041 "selection" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250663 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250668 13194139533781 true] [17592186250663 1110 #uuid "4792ce8e-51ae-5527-b281-d69c7574ea26" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250664 1034 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250664 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250664 1111 #uuid "7ee060b1-3746-5e0b-83ad-ec50cd9c83a2" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250665 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250665 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250665 1111 #uuid "8e15aa35-000e-57ad-a13f-5431f1957930" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250666 1034 "-\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250666 1111 #uuid "1699d48c-fb09-5584-bf02-fb59e39c4f5e" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250667 1034 "\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250667 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250667 1111 #uuid "e0e0fcc6-a4c0-5bd9-bce9-36959fcdcc35" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250668 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250668 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250668 1111 #uuid "8f4ba13e-21cc-539e-8498-077deeb957c6" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250669 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250670 13194139533781 true] [17592186250669 1089 "q-143638" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250669 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533781 true] [17592186250669 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/112ee04f02087fbf9f477a4cc002a7b24f7881e1ac2e37a1566ccc43e948cf0a.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250669 1113 #uuid "099318bb-f16c-592c-8396-8642f6dbb6d9" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250669 1145 "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{2\\pi }{\\pi }=2.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $2$ unit down. Hence, $D=-2.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=2+(-2)=0.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)-2.\n$$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250671 13194139533781 true] [17592186250670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250672 13194139533781 true] [17592186250670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250673 13194139533781 true] [17592186250670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250674 13194139533781 true] [17592186250670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250675 13194139533781 true] [17592186250670 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533781 true] [17592186250670 1041 "selection" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250670 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250674 13194139533781 true] [17592186250670 1110 #uuid "18c2557b-a4e9-54c8-b446-9bda2769a428" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250671 1034 "3" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250671 1103 #e