" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250694 1034 "-\\frac{2\\pi }{5}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250694 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250694 1111 #uuid "b856d1ba-4cd2-57e0-9ec0-38c7ecf1ab64" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250695 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250695 1111 #uuid "a2c2adbd-5475-5287-90ba-9d5e3581e2dc" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250696 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250696 1111 #uuid "a9b6ab24-a082-5ef0-9200-3272b8d65bf7" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250697 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250698 13194139533781 true] [17592186250697 1089 "q-143677" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250697 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533781 true] [17592186250697 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/7602d1695610361f28613d8bf3542056b2624f9b6b8980873f6fdebf802c6750.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3}+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250697 1113 #uuid "3090bea4-a609-5a53-a6eb-a8060c8d0e8b" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250697 1145 "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3}+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}(x+\\frac{3C}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+\\frac{3C}{2}$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}(x+\\frac{3C}{2}))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3}).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/015ca9336646a7545de842414ace2c2a695688e30653b2ed019000d69609d56d.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})$ by $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ units to the left. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3C}{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,⟹\\,C=(\\frac{\\pi }{4})(\\frac{2}{3})\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is in this interval, the value of $C$ is $\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250698 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250699 13194139533781 true] [17592186250698 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250700 13194139533781 true] [17592186250698 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250701 13194139533781 true] [17592186250698 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250702 13194139533781 true] [17592186250698 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250703 13194139533781 true] [17592186250698 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533781 true] [17592186250698 1041 "selection" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250698 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250703 13194139533781 true] [17592186250698 1110 #uuid "a13a5095-aa8b-5e41-9483-27f8aedf50a8" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250699 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250699 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250699 1111 #uuid "6b673c6a-01e8-5d9e-8f0f-74d7c698a37c" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250700 1034 "-\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250700 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250700 1111 #uuid "c3d5962b-c7d1-5864-858d-fe3f1d39738a" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250701 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250701 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250701 1111 #uuid "5babeeef-a8f1-511a-b58f-bed13852c167" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250702 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250702 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250702 1111 #uuid "c32bdca9-cd10-5d08-bf2a-49619ae4741c" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250703 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250703 1111 #uuid "1111f967-7f83-575f-ac96-99557c1be78b" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250704 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250705 13194139533781 true] [17592186250704 1089 "q-65550" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250704 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533781 true] [17592186250704 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/c904a1eb628e726647a6f655a567a0939f7b7d404f0b32c6c4b4adaeca847916.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B-D?$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250704 1113 #uuid "2a31794b-90ed-5858-8a23-bda34267af75" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250704 1145 "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{4\\pi }{5})}=\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $3$ units down. Hence, $D=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $B-D=(\\frac{5}{4})-(-3)=\\frac{5}{4}+3=\\frac{17}{4}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{5x}{4})-3.\n$$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250706 13194139533781 true] [17592186250705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250707 13194139533781 true] [17592186250705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250708 13194139533781 true] [17592186250705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250709 13194139533781 true] [17592186250705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250710 13194139533781 true] [17592186250705 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533781 true] [17592186250705 1041 "selection" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250705 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250710 13194139533781 true] [17592186250705 1110 #uuid "7d443759-daaa-55fa-bfa3-463af17a09d3" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250706 1034 "-\\frac{7}{4}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250706 1111 #uuid "b1c2c1eb-db74-5e2c-bd88-9f3da1804b2f" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250707 1034 "-\\frac{5}{4}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250707 1111 #uuid "b49b83fd-1776-57d2-abe2-14ebdae03ada" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250708 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250708 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250708 1111 #uuid "1f62e4b8-261e-5898-a374-81526ea71b04" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250709 1034 "4" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250709 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250709 1111 #uuid "31136edc-d135-5bc5-9b5d-0b937c221afe" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250710 1034 "\\frac{17}{4}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250710 1111 #uuid "d3ccaef8-8575-5851-a29a-8efa68f8a05e" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250711 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250712 13194139533781 true] [17592186250711 1089 "q-79195" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250711 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533781 true] [17592186250711 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/89efc20f1c6527d1bcd501f97ce585fb5a60e9791804f56d61f33653cf1a70d7.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250711 1113 #uuid "adbc630c-edd8-52e4-9bd9-f612c8f44da5" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250711 1145 "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3(x+\\frac{C}{3}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+\\frac{C}{3}$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3(x+\\frac{C}{3}))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/f8617da98ea9d9fb48b8fef588b624c6961a299233836fe433c1819b697ca0fb.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)$ by $0-(-\\frac{\\pi }{12})=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ units to the left. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{C}{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is in this interval, the value of $C$ is $\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250713 13194139533781 true] [17592186250712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250714 13194139533781 true] [17592186250712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250715 13194139533781 true] [17592186250712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250716 13194139533781 true] [17592186250712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250717 13194139533781 true] [17592186250712 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533781 true] [17592186250712 1041 "selection" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250712 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250714 13194139533781 true] [17592186250712 1110 #uuid "36837e76-b2da-51d2-a076-35871200dfc1" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250713 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250713 1111 #uuid "0a342a72-b5db-52a8-bbbc-4f6c459093e9" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250714 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250714 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533781 true] [17592186250714 1111 #uuid "c2abc93f-c5ef-5767-9f98-f5421b4b7328" 13194139533781 true] [17592186250715 1034 "\\frac